sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Buss, Anderson & Perry (2015) Biol. Bull., Dudgeon et al. (1999) Am. Nat. & Blackstone (1999) Syst. Biol. colonial hydroid pulsatile gastrovascular stolon network, anastomosis loop closure, and runner-to-sheet morphospace — MorphoEval overall 93.8/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2020-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net.py` (overall weighted score: 93.8/100, up from 53.0/100 in v1). The remediated script solves the coupled pulsatile polyp oscillator + Hagen-Poiseuille Kirchhoff gastrovascular network across V = 26 stolon/polyp nodes and E = 62 stolon segments (conservation error 1.42e-12); reproduces the Blackstone (1999) and Buss, Anderson & Perry (2015) runner-to-sheet continuum across polyp pumping gain eta in [0.35, 1.65] for planar meshedness alpha (Pearson r = 0.99886, RMSE = 0.0130, p = 3.74e-9) and coenosarc mat coverage (Pearson r = 0.99768, RMSE = 0.0213, p = 3.12e-8); captures the Podocoryna runner morph (alpha = 0.1064, b_1 = 5), 2,4-DNP redox uncoupling shift (alpha = 0.3404, b_1 = 16), Hydractinia dense sheet morph (alpha = 0.7872, b_1 = 37), and MgCl2 polyp-arrest regression control (alpha = 0.0000, b_1 = 0); and segments the SHA-256-locked Yale Peabody Museum Hydractinia symbiolongicarpus specimen (`YPM IZ 080458`, V = 332 polyps, b_1 = 514 loops, alpha = 0.7800, tissue coverage = 0.8918). Overall 93.8/100 (faithfulness 93.8, reproducibility 93.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 95, Morphological realism / specimen match 93, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 94, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/hydractinia_stolon_vascular_net_comparison.png: rendered output of 2020-badin-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net.py at 8871db0, image/png, 1150393 B, 2475×1530 px, artifact_sha256 feed403a8a81252c9e9f6a094576be6c10e7c5f019284aa5dde113f23d34a456 (sha256 feed403a8a81252c9e9f6a094576be6c10e7c5f019284aa5dde113f23d34a456), spec_fingerprint 89c0f33a7d88261f666404a05447dcbcee682836ef33db2cdc94324f94c96aa2. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 89c0f33a7d88261f666404a05447dcbcee682836ef33db2cdc94324f94c96aa2; artifact_sha256: feed403a8a81252c9e9f6a094576be6c10e7c5f019284aa5dde113f23d34a456; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/hydractinia_stolon_vascular_net/hydractinia_stolon_vascular_net_reference.json=db4c51ae3bdeb00a..., datasets/hydractinia_stolon_vascular_net/hydractinia_symbiolongicarpus_specimen.jpg=059b83cd797d0516..., datasets/hydractinia_stolon_vascular_net/paper_citations.bib=44b19ab180b9e27a..., datasets/hydractinia_stolon_vascular_net/scout_manifest.json=626e17690a5a1cd7...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-hydractinia-stolon-vascular-net-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Buss, Anderson & Perry (2015) Biol. Bull. 228:146-158 & Dudgeon et al. (1999) Am. Nat. 153:292-309 pulsatile polyp contraction oscillators V_p(t) = V_0 + Delta_V sin(omega_p t + phi_p) driving Hagen-Poiseuille gastrovascular lumen flow Q_ij = (pi r_ij^4 / (8 mu L_ij))(p_i - p_j) and endodermal wall shear stress tau_w = 4 mu |Q_ij| / (pi r_ij^3) | Blackstone (1999) Syst. Biol. 48:75-85 & Buss (2001) Evol. Dev. 3:311-322 heterochronic runner-to-sheet colonial hydroid morphospace continuum: low polyp pumping produces sparse Podocoryna runner trees (low planar meshedness alpha), 2,4-DNP redox uncoupling shifts runner colonies toward reticulate webs, and high Hydractinia pumping produces confluent anastomosed stolonal mats/sheets (alpha ~ 0.78) | Polyp excision or MgCl2 muscular contraction arrest (Delta_V_p = 0) eliminates gastrovascular flow and wall shear stress below tau_reg, triggering stolon lumen collapse and regression into empty chitinous perisarc tubes; reconstructed_in_script: Full weighted graph Laplacian Kirchhoff gastrovascular solver (`solve_gastrovascular_kirchhoff`) across V = 26 stolon/polyp nodes and E = 62 stolon segments verifying nodal volume conservation (error 1.42e-12 < 1e-11), flux antisymmetry (< 1e-14), and cubic-radius wall shear identity (< 1e-12) | 8-point polyp pumping gain sweep across eta in [0.35, 1.65] reproducing the runner-to-sheet planar meshedness continuum alpha (Pearson r = 0.99886, RMSE = 0.0130, p = 3.74e-9) and coenosarc mat area coverage (Pearson r = 0.99768, RMSE = 0.0213, p = 3.12e-8) | 5 canonical morphospace regimes: Podocoryna runner (eta = 0.55, alpha = 0.1064, b_1 = 5), 2,4-DNP redox-uncoupled shift (eta = 0.90, alpha = 0.3404, b_1 = 16, delta = +0.2340), Hydractinia intermediate web (eta = 1.25, alpha = 0.5745, b_1 = 27), Hydractinia mature stolonal sheet (eta = 1.65, alpha = 0.7872, b_1 = 37), and polyp-excision / MgCl2 contraction arrest regression control (eta = 0.0, surviving stolon fraction = 0.0, b_1 = 0) | Computer-vision segmentation of Yale Peabody Museum `hydractinia_symbiolongicarpus_specimen.jpg` (`YPM IZ 080458`, CC0) extracting coenosarc mat coverage 0.8918, V = 332 gastrovascular polyp cavities, E = 845 stolon links, b_1 = 514 closed anastomosed loops, planar meshedness alpha = 0.7800, and inter-polyp NND CV = 0.3022 (18.64 +- 5.63 px); transfer_boundary: 2D planar pulsatile Kirchhoff pipe network with shear-stress-gated lumen adaptation and Delaunay-coenosarc vascular graph extraction mapped to colonial hydroid stolonal mats; does_not_claim: Subcellular chitin synthase secretion kinetics or allorecognition histocompatibility (alr1/alr2) fusion/rejection signaling between genetically distinct colonies." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the planar gastrovascular stolonal network to allorecognition (alr1/alr2) histocompatibility signaling to model self-fusion vs non-self hyperplastic stolon rejection between neighboring colonies." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.938"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 100 Pass 2 Assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

